==English==

===Etymology===
[[Yiddish]] [[מענטש]] (mentsh), an honorable person, from German [[Mensch]] (person).

===Alternative spellings===
* [[mentsch]]
* [[mentsh]]
* [[mensch]]

===Noun===
'''mentch'''

# {{literally}} A [[human]] or [[person]].
# A person with [[integrity]] and concern for others.
# A [[gentleman]].

====Antonyms====
* [[imposter]]
* [[snob]]

